# src/apps/daemon/internal/foundation/crypto

## Purpose
Go cryptographic and TPM helpers used by configuration/runtime code; contains key wrapping, obfuscation, and platform-backed cryptographic support.

## Architectural role
- Daemon dependency band: `foundation` (rank 0; lower rank = deeper implementation).
- Cross-band imports may point only to a lower rank. Same-band imports are allowed when they remain within one architectural layer.

## Contents
- Direct files (16): `cfg_compiler.go`, `cfg_compiler_test.go`, `dpapi_stub.go`, `dpapi_test.go`, `dpapi_windows.go`, `tpm.go`, `tpm_envelope.go`, `tpm_envelope_lock_unix.go`, `tpm_envelope_lock_windows.go`, `tpm_envelope_store.go`, `tpm_envelope_store_test.go`, `tpm_envelope_test.go` …

## Interfaces and dependencies
- Go package: `crypto`.
- Notable exported surface: `CFGCompiler`, `CFGConn`, `Decrypt`, `DefaultTPMPolicy`, `Encrypt`, `ErrLegacyCutoff`, `ErrLegacyTPMSealingDisabled`, `ErrTPMKeyMigrationRequired`, `ErrUnsupportedTPMEnvelope`, `IsTPMAvailable` …
- Daemon-local dependencies: `internal/foundation/secrets`.
- Direct daemon callers: `cmd`, `internal/foundation/config`, `internal/runtime/proxy`.

## Invariants
- `foundation` code must not import a higher-rank daemon band.

